[size=6][b]Bigger Armies — more ground forces for your faction in SpaceBourne 2[/b][/size]

In SpaceBourne 2 your faction's forces are its generals, and each general leads 4 soldiers. A new faction gets 10 general slots, 5 for Ground Forces and 5 for Space Forces: 10 squads, 50 men. "Fifty men isn't exactly an army to conquer the galaxy." Bigger Armies gives your faction more general slots, so you can field twice as many men.

Version 0.1.1 · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/17]Nexus Mods page[/url] · UE4SS Lua mod · works alone or with the rest of the [url=#part-of-the-spacebourne-2-realism-set]realism set[/url].

[line]
[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]10 more general slots[/b] by default (5 Ground Forces, 5 Space Forces), on top of the game's own. Each slot is room for a general and 4 soldiers: 50 more men, 100 in all.
[*][b]The game's own way:[/b] the slots are added with the same function the station upgrade uses, so they look and work like the game's slots. Fill them as usual: recruit, promote a soldier to general, give them soldiers.
[*][b]Still costs you:[/b] every recruit costs 200 Faction Power and a daily fee, as in the game.
[*][b]Up to 110 men:[/b] the game stops recruiting at 110 people in total, so the mod never goes above 22 slots (22 squads of 5).
[*][b]Your faction first:[/b] nothing happens until you have founded your faction; the slots appear a few seconds after that, or after loading a save.
[*][b]On by default.[/b] No key needed.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]SpaceBourne 2 (Steam).
[*][url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]UE4SS 3.0.1[/url], a free script loader for Unreal Engine games.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[b]Option A (recommended):[/b] the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]SpaceBourne 2 Realism[/url] installer installs UE4SS and any mods of the set you pick.

[b]Option B, manual:[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]UE4SS 3.0.1[/url] into SpaceBourne 2\SB2\Binaries\Win64\.
[*]Download BiggerArmies-0.1.1.zip from the [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies/releases]releases[/url] and extract it into the game folder (...\steamapps\common\SpaceBourne 2\). It adds SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\BiggerArmies\; the enabled.txt inside turns it on.
[/list]

Uninstall: delete SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\BiggerArmies. The slots already added stay in your save and keep working; the game just stops getting new ones from the mod.

[line]
[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

Edit Mods\BiggerArmies\scripts\config.lua, then restart the game. Every line is optional.

[list]
[*]Enabled: false switches the mod off.
[*]ExtraGeneralSlots (10): general slots added on top of the game's own, 0–12. They come in pairs, one Ground Forces and one Space Forces general (the game adds them that way), so an odd number is rounded down. Each slot is room for 5 men.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Known limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]4 soldiers per general[/b] stays as in the game: the faction screen has exactly 4 soldier places per general, and the mod cannot change that screen.
[*][b]Lowering the setting[/b] does not remove slots you already have; the mod only adds.
[*][b]Battles with many squads[/b] put more soldiers on the field, which costs frames on slower PCs. That is the game's own cost; send fewer squads if a big battle runs slowly.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]

The game keeps your general slots in your faction's data and adds one with its own function when you upgrade your station. A few seconds after a load, the mod counts your slots, works out how many the game itself gave you, and calls that same function until you have the extra ones. It never removes anything. Details: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies/blob/mainDESIGN.md]DESIGN.md[/url].

[line]
[size=5][b]Part of the SpaceBourne 2 realism set[/b][/size]

Part of the realism set, built around [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url] as the core mod. HTR is not required: this mod works on its own or with any of the others. To install them all at once, use the installer: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]SpaceBourne 2 Realism[/url] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url]).

